Yuna, Kirito, Yuna,

3
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:25,570
Kirito, Mali, Mali, Kirito,
Vorumb, Tree, Kirito, Tree, Kirito,

4
00:00:25,653 --> 00:00:27,977
Yuna, Kirito, Tree, Kirito,
Zipo, Suguha, Yuna, Kirito, Yuna,

5
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:29,980
Kirito, confirmation.

6
00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:56,480
It's been almost two years
since this game of death began.

7
00:00:57,420 --> 00:00:59,040
I'm still going it alone.

8
00:00:59,980 --> 00:01:01,921
fighting solo on the front lines.

9
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:08,760
Akihiko Kayaba's out
there somewhere, watching.

10
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:11,435
I wonder what he's thinking right now.

11
00:01:16,660 --> 00:01:17,895
Guess I'll head home.

12
00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:30,900
c L .

13
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:49,617
I don't know what I'm saying,
but I don't know what I'm saying,

14
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:54,697
but I don't know what I'm saying.

15
00:01:54,780 --> 00:02:01,000
I'm afraid of the back of the back of
my back, but I'm still in the moment.

16
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:08,700
I've been looking for a long time,

17
00:02:09,180 --> 00:02:11,317
and I've been looking for a long time.

18
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:12,740
Here is my heart,

19
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:16,917
and I've been looking

20
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:22,457
for a long time.

21
00:02:51,140 --> 00:02:57,160
I wanna know what we do, I'll
give you everything I have

22
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:22,771
You've got to be kidding.

23
00:03:43,020 --> 00:03:44,217
No way.

24
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:46,420
This is an Skills rare item.

25
00:03:47,220 --> 00:03:50,338
Holy crap, this is the first
time I've ever seen one.

26
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:54,971
Hey, Kirito, don't you already
have all the money you need?

27
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:59,077
I'll buy it, but I'm saying, wouldn't
you rather have it for dinner?

28
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:03,320
Sure, it's just, well, who knows
if I'll ever get another one.

29
00:04:03,420 --> 00:04:04,260
So keep it.

30
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:05,420
What's the point?

31
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:10,645
Look, to prepare an item like this, you
need to have a high enough cooking skill.

32
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:11,880
Yeah, you're right.

33
00:04:12,060 --> 00:04:13,648
If we try, we just burn it.

34
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:17,710
Kirito.

35
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:24,620
I've got my chef.

36
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:26,080
Uh, what chef?

37
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:30,380
Hey, Asuna's here.

38
00:04:30,660 --> 00:04:33,425
Seeing you in a dump like
this is beyond weird.

39
00:04:33,740 --> 00:04:34,570
Oh, save it.

40
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:36,497
I came to see if you were still alive.

41
00:04:36,580 --> 00:04:38,977
You know, it's almost time
for the next boss raid.

42
00:04:39,060 --> 00:04:40,337
I'm on your friend list.

43
00:04:40,420 --> 00:04:42,957
If you want to know I'm
alive, just check that.

44
00:04:43,040 --> 00:04:45,040
Whatever, now I know you're alive.

45
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:46,788
Anyway, what are you up to?

46
00:04:47,020 --> 00:04:48,697
What's all this about a chef?

47
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:50,040
Oh, yeah, that.

48
00:04:50,380 --> 00:04:53,262
I was wondering what your
cooking skill level is.

49
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:55,130
Hmm.

50
00:04:55,213 --> 00:04:56,960
Totally maxed it out last week. What?

51
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:58,280
Cool, huh?

52
00:04:59,140 --> 00:05:02,300
Well, if you're that
good, I need a favor. Hmm?

53
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:11,480
You got a Rika rabbit? I'll trade you.

54
00:05:11,820 --> 00:05:16,349
All you have to do is cook it up for
me, and I'll let you have a little bite.

55
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:18,980
Half. Deal?

56
00:05:21,460 --> 00:05:22,560
Yeah, deal.

57
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:24,360
All right!

58
00:05:27,980 --> 00:05:28,810
Sorry, pal.

59
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:30,097
You heard the lady.

60
00:05:30,180 --> 00:05:31,177
Guess I'm keeping it.

61
00:05:31,260 --> 00:05:33,717
Yeah, but you could at least
let me taste it, right?

62
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:35,157
I thought we were tight, man.

63
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:37,737
I'll write a review for
you, but only two pages.

64
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:38,650
Promise.

65
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:41,960
Damn, that is cold.

66
00:05:43,580 --> 00:05:45,760
So, where am I going to cook it?

67
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:48,117
Oh, well...

68
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:50,177
I'm guessing not your place, right?

69
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:52,660
You even own any cookware? Mama.

70
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:54,130
Okay,

71
00:05:54,213 --> 00:05:56,037
because the main ingredient is special,

72
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:59,238
I won't have a problem if
we used my place this time.

73
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:02,360
Thank you for escorting me.

74
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:03,800
You may go.

75
00:06:04,260 --> 00:06:08,966
I'm sorry, ma 'am, but I can't allow you
to go home with such a shady character.

76
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:13,312
I don't know the extent of his shadiness,

77
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:15,325
But I know he's quite skilled.

78
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:18,280
In fact, he's ten levels
above you, Kuradeel.

79
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:21,160
Are you implying I'm inferior to him?

80
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,120
Oh, I know.

81
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:25,498
He's one of those beaters, isn't he?

82
00:06:26,300 --> 00:06:27,130
Yeah.

83
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:28,120
What if I am?

84
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:29,917
You shouldn't go with him, ma 'am.

85
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,237
All him and his kind care
about are themselves.

86
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:35,791
You can't expect anything good
to come from scum like that.

87
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:37,620
Hey, what's going on?

88
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:39,477
That's Lightning Flash Asuna.

89
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:40,390
You're right.

90
00:06:40,473 --> 00:06:41,437
She's really cute.

91
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:44,880
Listen, I'm second-in-command here.

92
00:06:45,140 --> 00:06:47,100
I am ordering you to go home.

93
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:51,880
Are you sure about this?

94
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:53,040
Of course!

95
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:04,370
Whoa.

96
00:07:04,453 --> 00:07:05,966
There's hardly anyone around.

97
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:08,180
It's really cool.

98
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:11,384
If you like it so much,
why don't you move here?

99
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:14,873
I don't know, this floor seems
way out of my price range.

100
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:18,217
Anyway, what's the deal
with that guy back there?

101
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:20,241
He was mad-dogging me like crazy.

102
00:07:20,620 --> 00:07:22,360
Oh, he's just my bodyguard.

103
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:26,602
The guild's new policy says all
higher-ups have to have an escort.

104
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:28,500
It's lame.

105
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:31,537
The guild didn't have all these
rules and regulations before.

106
00:07:31,620 --> 00:07:33,208
We used to be really small.

107
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:36,440
But then, more and more people joined up.

108
00:07:36,820 --> 00:07:41,585
After that, when we became the strongest
guild, everything started getting weird.

109
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:47,608
Well, I'm probably making a
bigger deal out of it than it is.

110
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:49,832
Anyway, we better hurry.

111
00:07:50,020 --> 00:07:51,077
It's getting dark.

112
00:07:51,160 --> 00:07:52,200
Oh, okay.

113
00:07:56,280 --> 00:07:58,520
Wow, you've got a killer pad.

114
00:08:01,580 --> 00:08:04,160
Hey, how much did all this cost?

115
00:08:05,960 --> 00:08:09,240
The room and the furniture
cost around $4 million coal.

116
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,765
Anyway, make yourself at home.

117
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:13,560
Uh, sure.

118
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:17,000
Holy moly.

119
00:08:19,140 --> 00:08:20,160
Four million.

120
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:22,620
Man, that's a lot of coal.

121
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:27,522
I'm sure I've earned that much,
too, but blowing it all on a flat?

122
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:36,428
Are you going to take
off your coat or what?

123
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:38,620
Oh, yeah, sorry.

124
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:46,420
So this is a legendary Skills ingredient.

125
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:49,277
Okay, how do you want this cooked up?

126
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:51,997
I thought I'd leave that
decision up to the chef.

127
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:55,520
In that case, how about
we make it into a stew?

128
00:08:57,160 --> 00:09:00,101
Rika, that's pretty much
the definition of a stew.

129
00:09:11,400 --> 00:09:15,459
In real life, there'd be a lot more
steps involved in preparing this.

130
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:18,860
Cooking an SAO is so simple.

131
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:21,454
Believe it or not, it's kind of boring.

132
00:09:23,720 --> 00:09:25,140
That takes care of that.

133
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:26,614
Now for the next step.

134
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,882
I was thinking about making
a couple side dishes.

135
00:09:55,900 --> 00:10:00,724
I've been here two years, and this is the
first time I've ever eaten Skills food.

136
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:03,880
I'm so happy I survived
long enough to eat that.

137
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:05,580
Yeah, me too.

138
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:08,260
It's so weird.

139
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:10,617
Sometimes, I don't know,

140
00:10:10,700 --> 00:10:14,177
I get this feeling that like
I've lived here my entire life.

141
00:10:14,260 --> 00:10:15,672
You ever feel like that?

142
00:10:16,140 --> 00:10:17,740
Yeah, almost all the time.

143
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:21,697
In fact, there's days I don't even
think about the real world at all.

144
00:10:21,780 --> 00:10:23,140
And it's not just me.

145
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:24,670
These days,

146
00:10:24,753 --> 00:10:26,237
more and more people
don't seem to care about

147
00:10:26,320 --> 00:10:29,397
clearing the game and getting
back to the real world.

148
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:33,137
I notice there's not that many players
out there fighting on the front lines.

149
00:10:33,220 --> 00:10:35,080
Maybe 500, if that.

150
00:10:35,780 --> 00:10:37,880
I guess they're used to it.

151
00:10:38,460 --> 00:10:39,872
They don't care anymore.

152
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:44,340
Yeah, well, I want to go back.

153
00:10:45,580 --> 00:10:48,200
I mean, there's things I haven't done yet.

154
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:49,360
I have to.

155
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:51,600
I know how you feel.

156
00:10:51,820 --> 00:10:55,117
And when you stop to consider
it, there's everyone else, right?

157
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:57,117
All the people who still count on us?

158
00:10:57,200 --> 00:10:59,376
If we give up, it's not fair to them.

159
00:11:03,380 --> 00:11:05,260
Uh-uh, don't go there.

160
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:07,190
What?

161
00:11:07,273 --> 00:11:09,605
I've seen that same look
on guys' faces before,

162
00:11:09,700 --> 00:11:12,288
and always right before
they proposed to me.

163
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:16,371
You should see your face.

164
00:11:16,500 --> 00:11:18,971
I guess you never had a girlfriend before.

165
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:22,140
Eh, whatever, I'm a solo player.

166
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:30,017
And you're okay with that?

167
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:32,218
You don't ever want to join a guild?

168
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:36,473
I know how the beta players
don't fit in with the guilds.

169
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:41,880
But ever since we got to Floor 70,
things are getting more dangerous.

170
00:11:42,340 --> 00:11:45,105
The monster algorithms
are even more irregular.

171
00:11:48,100 --> 00:11:50,688
There are things a solo
player can't handle.

172
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:52,259
Unexpected things.

173
00:11:52,860 --> 00:11:55,095
Sometimes warping out isn't an option.

174
00:11:55,740 --> 00:11:57,860
Yeah, well, I'm pretty careful.

175
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:01,000
I work better by myself anyway.

176
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:05,257
Besides, most of the time, instead of
helping, party members just get in the way.

177
00:12:05,340 --> 00:12:06,170
Oh, yeah?

178
00:12:09,620 --> 00:12:10,450
My bad.

179
00:12:10,533 --> 00:12:12,380
Everyone except for you. Good.

180
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:16,947
So, what do you say you
and me team up again?

181
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:20,377
Black's my lucky color this week anyway.

182
00:12:20,460 --> 00:12:21,290
Hold up a sec.

183
00:12:21,660 --> 00:12:23,517
Don't you have stuff you
have to do for your guild?

184
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:24,797
You can't just bail on him.

185
00:12:24,880 --> 00:12:27,377
It's not like we have any
leveling quotas to meet.

186
00:12:27,460 --> 00:12:29,097
Well then, what about your bodyguard?

187
00:12:29,180 --> 00:12:30,356
I'll just ditch him.

188
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:56,620
The front lines are dangerous, though.

189
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:03,220
Okay, fine.

190
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:14,820
Well, I suppose thanks are in
order for the meal, so thank you.

191
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:16,760
Thank you for cooking it.

192
00:13:16,920 --> 00:13:17,861
Maybe next time.

193
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:19,320
What am I saying?

194
00:13:19,580 --> 00:13:22,237
I'll never get my hands on
something like that again.

195
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:23,150
No way.

196
00:13:23,233 --> 00:13:26,471
You can make anything yummy if
you have the skills to cook.

197
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:36,297
Looking at this world and seeing
what it's become since we got here,

198
00:13:36,380 --> 00:13:39,439
Is this really what Akihiko
Kayaba wanted to create?

199
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:51,120
Where is she?

200
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:05,940
What is this thing?

201
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,560
Hmm, squishy.

202
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:20,550
Ow.

203
00:14:31,380 --> 00:14:32,380
Um, hey.

204
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:33,856
Good morning, Asuna.

205
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:41,590
What's wrong?

206
00:14:45,140 --> 00:14:46,957
Why are you behaving like this, ma 'am?

207
00:14:47,040 --> 00:14:48,569
I'm only following orders.

208
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:51,197
Please, let's go back to headquarters.

209
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:53,580
I won't, especially not with you.

210
00:14:53,760 --> 00:14:57,017
And why were you lurking around
my house in the morning, huh?

211
00:14:57,100 --> 00:15:00,159
You have a bad habit of
leaving without any warning.

212
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:01,517
So for the past month,

213
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:04,477
part of my mission has been to
keep an eye on you in Selmburg.

214
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:05,390
What?

215
00:15:05,473 --> 00:15:06,303
Who ordered this?

216
00:15:06,386 --> 00:15:07,792
It wasn't the commander.

217
00:15:07,920 --> 00:15:10,977
With all due respect, ma 'am,
my mission is to guard you,

218
00:15:11,060 --> 00:15:13,577
no matter where you are,
including your home.

219
00:15:13,660 --> 00:15:15,189
No, it doesn't, you idiot!

220
00:15:16,680 --> 00:15:20,621
I wish you would be a little more
understanding about this, ma 'am.

221
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:23,134
Now then, let's return to headquarters.

222
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:31,857
Sorry, but I'll be borrowing your
second-in-command for the day,

223
00:15:31,940 --> 00:15:34,469
so you'll just have to
make do without her.

224
00:15:34,860 --> 00:15:37,331
I'll take responsibility for her security.

225
00:15:37,940 --> 00:15:40,697
Don't worry, it's not like
we're going on a boss raid.

226
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:41,620
You can go.

227
00:15:41,760 --> 00:15:43,113
She'll be fine with me.

228
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:44,190
Insolent punk!

229
00:15:44,420 --> 00:15:46,080
Do you know who I am?

230
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:48,957
I'm a member of the glorious
Knights of the Blood Oath.

231
00:15:49,040 --> 00:15:51,697
A low-level player like
you couldn't protect her.

232
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:53,956
I can do a better job of it than you.

233
00:15:56,280 --> 00:15:57,940
You've got a big mouth, kid.

234
00:15:58,220 --> 00:16:02,514
So I'm going to give you a chance to
prove just how tough you really are.

235
00:16:08,020 --> 00:16:10,100
Are you sure? Don't worry.

236
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:13,431
I'll tell the commander how this happened.

237
00:16:19,140 --> 00:16:21,377
Please move to a safe distance, ma 'am.

238
00:16:21,460 --> 00:16:26,107
I'm going to prove beyond any doubt that
I am the only one who can protect you.

239
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:33,337
Kirito's gonna duel a guy from
the Knights of the Blood Oath.

240
00:16:33,420 --> 00:16:34,949
This will be fun to watch.

241
00:17:19,900 --> 00:17:21,680
I can't believe it!

242
00:17:27,660 --> 00:17:30,240
Holy crap, he destroyed his sword.

243
00:17:30,400 --> 00:17:31,518
How did he do that?

244
00:17:32,800 --> 00:17:36,577
If you want to try again with another
weapon, I'll be glad to take you on.

245
00:17:36,660 --> 00:17:38,300
Or we can call it a day.

246
00:17:48,260 --> 00:17:49,090
Asuna!

247
00:17:51,680 --> 00:17:53,700
I don't know how, but he cheated!

248
00:17:53,980 --> 00:17:55,980
You saw how he destroyed my sword!

249
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:58,057
He must have used some kind of trick!

250
00:17:58,140 --> 00:18:02,199
There's no other way I could have
lost to a pathetic beater like him!

251
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:04,030
Kuradeel,

252
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:07,077
as second-in-command of the
Knights of the Blood Oath,

253
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:10,042
I'm relieving you of your
duties as my bodyguard.

254
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:14,028
You're to return to headquarters
and wait for further orders.

255
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:16,220
You can't be serious!

256
00:18:16,660 --> 00:18:17,580
Damn you!

257
00:18:31,420 --> 00:18:32,250
Teleport.

258
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:33,670
Ransom.

259
00:18:47,260 --> 00:18:48,380
I'm so sorry.

260
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:50,817
I didn't mean to drag you into that.

261
00:18:50,900 --> 00:18:52,340
No, it's no big deal.

262
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:55,140
I'm worried about you. Are you okay?

263
00:18:55,660 --> 00:18:56,490
Yeah, I am.

264
00:18:57,040 --> 00:18:59,297
The guild's getting on my nerves is all.

265
00:18:59,380 --> 00:19:02,377
Maybe because I've been so
focused on clearing the game.

266
00:19:02,460 --> 00:19:06,460
Or maybe because I'm so demanding
of the other members in the guild.

267
00:19:07,700 --> 00:19:08,820
Yeah, I get that.

268
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:11,416
But you didn't have much of a choice.

269
00:19:11,500 --> 00:19:12,330
Think about it.

270
00:19:12,413 --> 00:19:13,817
If you'd done things any different,

271
00:19:13,900 --> 00:19:17,371
you think your guild would have
gotten as far as they have?

272
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:20,020
I mean, what do I know?

273
00:19:20,140 --> 00:19:22,417
I just mess around as
a solo player, right?

274
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:27,029
The thing is, if you take a day off to
team up with a loser like me, so what?

275
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:29,006
That's your decision to make.

276
00:19:29,180 --> 00:19:32,121
In my opinion, no one's
got the right to complain.

277
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:33,110
Screw him.

278
00:19:36,940 --> 00:19:39,377
Wow, thank you for your
opinion on the subject.

279
00:19:39,460 --> 00:19:43,457
Okay, I accept your offer and I'll
be taking a day off from the guild.

280
00:19:43,540 --> 00:19:45,077
You can play forward today.

281
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:45,990
Huh?

282
00:19:46,073 --> 00:19:48,697
Wait a second, aren't we supposed
to take turns as forward?

283
00:19:48,780 --> 00:19:50,760
Sorry, it's my day off, remember?

284
00:19:51,120 --> 00:19:52,120
Oh, come on!

285
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:22,657
Having someone along who knows how
to fight sure makes things easier.

286
00:20:22,740 --> 00:20:24,093
Switch with me, Kirito!

287
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:25,420
Yeah, right!

288
00:20:44,300 --> 00:20:45,540
Kirito, look.

289
00:20:53,440 --> 00:20:55,300
Is that what I think it is?

290
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:56,790
Uh-huh.

291
00:20:57,940 --> 00:20:59,620
We found the boss room.

292
00:21:00,460 --> 00:21:01,600
What do we do?

293
00:21:01,820 --> 00:21:03,740
You think we should look inside?

294
00:21:04,500 --> 00:21:06,088
Well, we came all this way.

295
00:21:06,340 --> 00:21:09,097
Besides, boss monsters never
leave the rooms they guard.

296
00:21:09,180 --> 00:21:11,817
I think we'll be okay
if we just take a peek.

297
00:21:11,900 --> 00:21:12,760
Oh, okay.

298
00:21:13,420 --> 00:21:16,260
Have a teleport crystal
ready, just in case.

299
00:21:16,900 --> 00:21:17,730
Right.

300
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:22,020
Okay, are you ready? Mm-hmm.

301
00:21:38,740 --> 00:21:41,780
I don't know.

302
00:22:01,820 --> 00:22:03,520
I'll be on, I'll be on.

303
00:22:18,380 --> 00:22:21,997
I heard the sound of the sound?

304
00:22:23,560 --> 00:22:29,040
It's a little sad to me. Yeah,

305
00:22:29,540 --> 00:22:30,977
yeah, yeah,

306
00:22:31,060 --> 00:22:38,060
yeah,

307
00:22:41,960 --> 00:22:48,960
yeah.

308
00:22:59,340 --> 00:23:02,577
I can't believe this love.

309
00:23:02,660 --> 00:23:05,100
In the front of my eyes,

310
00:23:05,540 --> 00:23:09,940
I can't believe it.

311
00:23:13,180 --> 00:23:17,220
Even if I'm dreaming, I can't believe it.

312
00:23:17,900 --> 00:23:20,677
I'm still in the middle of my heart.

313
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:37,860
Next time, the blue-eyed demon.
